.card.mb-4.border-warning
  .card-header.bg-warning-subtle
    %h2.h5.mb-0 Gaps in employment
  .card-body
    %p.small.text-muted
      A gap can mean continuous employment with missing connection, or that #{casual_name} left and came back.
    - gaps.each do |gap|
      - earlier = tenures_by_id[gap.earlier_tenure_id]
      - later = tenures_by_id[gap.later_tenure_id]
      .border.rounded.p-3.mb-3
        %p.mb-2
          Gap from
          %strong= gap.gap_started_at.to_date
          to
          %strong= gap.gap_ended_at.to_date
          between
          %strong= earlier&.position&.display_name || "earlier tenure"
          and
          %strong= later&.position&.display_name || "later tenure"
        %p.mb-3
          Should we connect these tenures, or did #{casual_name} leave and then come back to being employed?
        .d-flex.flex-wrap.gap-2.align-items-center
          - if can_correct
            = button_to "Connect these tenures",
                        connect_gap_organization_company_teammate_employment_history_correction_path(organization, @teammate),
                        method: :post,
                        params: { earlier_tenure_id: gap.earlier_tenure_id, later_tenure_id: gap.later_tenure_id },
                        class: "btn btn-sm btn-warning",
                        form: { data: { turbo: false } }
          - else
            %span.btn.btn-sm.btn-outline-secondary.disabled{aria: { disabled: true }}
              Connect these tenures
            %i.bi.bi-exclamation-triangle.text-warning{data: {bs_toggle: "tooltip", bs_title: disabled_tooltip}, title: disabled_tooltip, "aria-label": disabled_tooltip}
          %span.btn.btn-sm.btn-outline-secondary.disabled{aria: { disabled: true }}
            Leave as boomerang (no change)
